Data quality tests verify SCD Type 2 integrity per business key: exactly one current record per key, no duplicate versions, and valid from/to date ranges; key columns are not null.
The framework fails (or flags, per configured severity) the execution when critical data quality rules are violated.
Every model execution is recorded in the audit table with start time, end time, status (RUNNING / SUCCESS / FAILED / SKIPPED) and duration, plus batch and run identifiers.
Failed or skipped executions are diagnosable through dbt logs and audit records (status and error message captured).
Data quality tests are generic and reusable across multiple SCD Type 2 models.
